            <div xml:id="d417">

                <pb facs="0702" n="676" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v16/pg676"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">396.1 GE/5–354: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Department of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-05-03T14:00:00+01:00">May 3, 1954—2 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Secto 75. Repeated information Paris 169.
                        Chauvel tells us that violent attacks
                    against Dien Bien Phu have suddenly stopped. French <pb facs="0703" n="677"
                        xml:id="pg677"/> are not certain what this means since they believe Viet
                    Minh has capability of carrying the fortress by storm. They suspect that attacks
                    against Dien Bien Phu are being orchestrated with Geneva negotiations with
                    signals being called from Geneva.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Dulles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
